# Room Flow stack

Do not change this stack. Do not suggest other backend frameworks unless explicitly asked.

## Back-end

- C#, .NET 10, ASP.NET Core Web API
- Entity Framework Core, LINQ, Dapper
- MediatR, CQRS, REST APIs

## Architecture

- Clean Architecture: Domain, Application, Infrastructure, Api
- SOLID principles
- Microservices: keep a modular backend while the product is a single domain (rooms / bookings); split later only if needed

## Conventions

- Thin REST controllers: send MediatR commands/queries, no direct database access
- CQRS: commands and queries go through MediatR
- Default data access: EF Core + LINQ (reads and writes)
- Dapper: raw SQL only when a query is too heavy or does not map well to EF
- Dependencies point inward: Api → Application/Infrastructure; Infrastructure implements Application interfaces; Domain has no infrastructure dependencies
